<article class="env-lemma" id="0ED5">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0ED5">Lemma <span data-tag="0ED5">68.25.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a locally Noetherian and universally catenary scheme. Let $\delta : S \to \mathbf{Z}$ be a dimension function. Let $X$ be a decent algebraic space over $S$ such that the structure morphism $X \to S$ is locally of finite type. Let $\delta _ X : |X| \to \mathbf{Z}$ be the map sending $x$ to $\delta (f(x))$ plus the transcendence degree of $x/f(x)$. Then $\delta _ X$ is a dimension function on $|X|$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\varphi : U \to X$ be a surjective étale morphism where $U$ is a scheme. Then the similarly defined function $\delta _ U$ is a dimension function on $U$ by Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/02JW" data-tag="02JW">29.53.3</a>. On the other hand, by the definition of relative transcendence degree in (Morphisms of Spaces, Definition <a href="/tag/04NM" data-tag="04NM">67.33.1</a>) we see that $\delta _ U(u) = \delta _ X(\varphi (u))$. 
    <p>
      Let $x \leadsto x'$ be a specialization of points in $|X|$. by Lemma <a href="/tag/03IL" data-tag="03IL">68.12.2</a> we can find a specialization $u \leadsto u'$ of points of $U$ with $\varphi (u) = x$ and $\varphi (u') = x'$. Moreover, we see that $x = x'$ if and only if $u = u'$, see Lemma <a href="/tag/03K5" data-tag="03K5">68.12.1</a>. Thus the fact that $\delta _ U$ is a dimension function implies that $\delta _ X$ is a dimension function, see Topology, Definition <a href="/tag/02I9" data-tag="02I9">5.20.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>